WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:07.470
SCP-049, also known as The Plague Doctor,
is an SCP Foundation fan favorite.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:12.360
This charming anomalous surgeon can terrify
with a glance and kill with a touch.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.710
In terms of his origins, his methods, and
his thought processes around a disease he

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:22.000
calls “The Pestilence”, this is one of
the most mysterious SCPs out there.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.699
And thankfully, we didn’t have to investigate
this one alone.

00:00:25.699 --> 00:00:31.830
We made a community post asking you, the fans
of SCP Explained, to give us your questions

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:36.320
and theories about the good doctor that we
all hope doesn’t give house calls - and

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:37.930
you didn’t disappoint.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:42.870
Let’s grab our masks and hand sanitizer,
and take a look at what you had to say about

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:44.570
SCP-049.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:47.410
First, the Questions:

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:51.990
Bob Candle asked, “Why does he refuse to
tell researchers about the pestilence?”

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:56.460
That’s a good question, and also one of
the biggest mysteries surrounding 049’s

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:57.460
lore.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:02.300
For the uninitiated, “The Pestilence”
- also known as the Great Dying - is the nickname

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:08.740
given to an unknown disease that SCP-049 has
dedicated his life to curing, whatever curing

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:09.940
means to him.

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:15.469
When asked by Foundation researchers, 049
refuses to give up even the most basic information

00:01:15.469 --> 00:01:22.069
about The Pestilence - such as how he diagnoses
it, what its effects are, or how it’s transmitted.

00:01:22.069 --> 00:01:26.820
It seems that part of the reason that 049
refuses to tell researchers about it is that

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:31.999
he apparently assumes that they, as fellow
doctors, inherently know what he’s talking

00:01:31.999 --> 00:01:34.109
about when he brings up The Pestilence.

00:01:34.109 --> 00:01:39.630
He has acted with confusion and frustration
during questioning and 049 seems to believe

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:43.950
that The Pestilence is such common knowledge
among medical practitioners that it would

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:48.679
be a waste of time to explain it - if he even
has the words to do so.

00:01:48.679 --> 00:01:53.670
Dat Gamer 56 asked, “Why is he so cooperative
if humans have the “Pestilence” he wants

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:55.119
to cure so bad?”

00:01:55.119 --> 00:01:59.939
One of the most remarkable things about 049
is how reasonable he’s been with Foundation

00:01:59.939 --> 00:02:01.360
staff in the past.

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:06.469
He’s polite, friendly, and treats his jailers
as equals - when he’s not murdering them

00:02:06.469 --> 00:02:08.450
and turning them into zombies.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:13.459
But this is a good question - if he believes
humans have The Pestilence, why is he so cooperative

00:02:13.459 --> 00:02:14.459
with them?

00:02:14.459 --> 00:02:20.030
Thankfully, the answer here is simple: While
049 believes that The Pestilence is widespread,

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:22.560
he doesn’t believe that every human is carrying
it.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:27.250
In fact, when he was first contained by the
Foundation and brought into an SCP facility,

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:31.650
he complimented the staff on how little Pestilence
there was inside the building compared to

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:32.780
the outside.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:37.829
While we don’t know what leads 049 to think
a person is healthy or diseased, we do know

00:02:37.829 --> 00:02:42.660
there is a distinction, and he’s cooperative
with those he sees as healthy.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:47.860
Star Doggo Gaming asked, “How would he interact
with 610, aka The Flesh That Hates?

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:51.330
I wonder if he would view the infected as
pestilence?”

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:52.590
Another great question.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:58.750
610 is an extremely dangerous Sarkic SCP that
presents as a zombie-like virus that causes

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:01.209
horrific fleshy mutations.

00:03:01.209 --> 00:03:05.739
Because of the extremely high infection rate
of the Flesh That Hates, it’s been quarantined

00:03:05.739 --> 00:03:09.140
in its present location in the isolated Siberian
wilderness.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:14.959
While it would be too dangerous to bring anyone
or anything into contact with The Flesh, we’re

00:03:14.959 --> 00:03:19.079
betting that 049 would find The Flesh utterly
repulsive.

00:03:19.079 --> 00:03:23.850
Whether even he would actually be able to
cure this horrific infection is another question.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:28.210
The Flesh that Hates is best left alone at
all costs.

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:35.079
Mcipher50 asked, “SCP-049's notebook appears
to be written in a language no human can decipher,

00:03:35.079 --> 00:03:39.359
Could another SCP like 343 or 662 decode the
notebook?”

00:03:39.359 --> 00:03:42.799
The answer to this is a solid… maybe.

00:03:42.799 --> 00:03:48.200
These two SCPs - known as God and Mr. Deeds,
respectively - may be able to translate the

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:52.040
contents of 049’s mysterious, leather-bound
notebook.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:56.569
The problem is, given that we’ve seen 049
is a pretty terrible doctor when it comes

00:03:56.569 --> 00:04:01.209
to anything other than raising mutant zombies
from the dead, the contents of his notebook

00:04:01.209 --> 00:04:05.980
might just be as useless as the interviews
with him have proven to be.

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:10.690
That said, it probably is worth a try, just
to find out if he’s actually been pretending

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:12.660
to write this whole time.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:18.220
GreenAngelSnake YT asked, “Do other living
creatures like pigs, cats or literally any

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:21.579
animal have this thing he calls ‘the Pestilence’?

00:04:21.579 --> 00:04:24.430
What even are the living things that he considers
cured?”

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:29.830
To the best of our knowledge, 049 only believes
humans can contract The Pestilence.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:31.169
How do we know this?

00:04:31.169 --> 00:04:33.680
This leads us to our next question.

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:38.389
Mia the Hotdog asked, “If he touches the
Immortal Lizard, will the lizard die and be

00:04:38.389 --> 00:04:43.210
rid of disease, or will the lizard be immune,
or will it attack the doctor?”

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:49.300
The Foundation did attempt to terminate 682
with 049, but the effort was unsuccessful.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:55.500
049, when encountering the lizard, commented
that only humans can contract the Pestilence.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:59.940
When he tried to touch 682, the lizard swiped
at him with its claws.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:05.620
049 then requested to leave and later interviews
revealed that the plague doctor felt “emotionally

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:08.919
disturbed” by his time with 682.

00:05:08.919 --> 00:05:12.599
Gamer Duck YT asked, “Where did he originally
come from?”

00:05:12.599 --> 00:05:18.110
While evidence suggests that 049 is extremely
old and very well traveled, he was first discovered

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:22.200
by the Foundation in the town of Montauban
in southern France.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:26.460
Given that he speaks fluent Medieval French
as his first language, it’s safe to assume

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:31.819
that France is probably his country of origin
and could have existed for hundreds of years,

00:05:31.819 --> 00:05:33.230
if not longer.

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:38.699
Interestingly, his famous plague doctor appearance
is more similar to those first worn by Italian

00:05:38.699 --> 00:05:45.349
doctors in the 17th century, which only deepens
the mystery of SCP-049.

00:05:45.349 --> 00:05:49.670
Garret Eborn asked, “Why does he insist
that he isn’t doing harm when he’s clearly

00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:51.990
in violation of his Hippocratic Oath?”

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:57.940
049 does seem to regret the harm he causes,
but he also believes that small sacrifices

00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:01.259
are necessary in the quest to cure The Pestilence.

00:06:01.259 --> 00:06:06.139
Also, a fun little history lesson - Given
that 049’s knowledge of medicine appears

00:06:06.139 --> 00:06:10.979
to be medieval - meaning potentially as early
as the 5th century - he actually would have

00:06:10.979 --> 00:06:15.970
predated the Hippocratic Oath coming into
universal use by doctors, which didn’t become

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:21.530
widespread until the 19th century - despite
the Oath itself first being created around

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:23.120
400 BC.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:28.070
Phoenix Fain asked, “If he was to wear gloves
of any kind would he still kill you?”

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:30.690
All evidence seems to point to “No.”

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:35.910
Only skin-to-skin contact with 049 is fatal,
so a good pair of gloves could really be a

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:36.910
lifesaver.

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:41.599
Alice Verdugo, “What would happen if he
went one on one with the shy guy?

00:06:41.599 --> 00:06:43.919
Would he "cure" him or not do anything?“

00:06:43.919 --> 00:06:50.409
While we can’t know for sure, because SCP-096
aka the Shy Guy isn’t human, it’s likely

00:06:50.409 --> 00:06:53.750
that 049 wouldn’t even consider him infected.

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:58.629
If the two came into contact, it would probably
result in a stalemate, much like the time

00:06:58.629 --> 00:07:01.900
SCP-096 faced off against SCP-682.

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:09.810
However, if it did come to blows between the
two, 096 is undeniably a much more dangerous

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:14.729
combatant, and may be able to narrowly defeat
the Plague Doctor in a direct confrontation

00:07:14.729 --> 00:07:16.750
while in its rage state.

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:20.879
Anything Goes asked, “If he died, could
he bring himself back to life, or have something

00:07:20.879 --> 00:07:23.159
prepared to bring himself back to life?”

00:07:23.159 --> 00:07:28.820
Like a lot of anomalies, it seems that 049
is abnormally hard to kill, given that he’s

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:31.419
seemingly impervious to most physical damage.

00:07:31.419 --> 00:07:36.870
However, seeing as 049’s resurrection is
both a lengthy medical process, and never

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:41.290
brings its subjects back correctly, it’s
likely that if someone could successfully

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:45.259
put 049 down, he wouldn’t get back up.

00:07:45.259 --> 00:07:49.940
ImNotComing asked, “We know that doctors
are wearing masks to protect patients but

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:52.680
is his mask part of his skull or face?”

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:58.310
All of 049’s clothes, including his Plague
Doctor mask, are technically part of his body.

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:03.259
The mask is part of its bone structure, and
the other clothes are like layers of skin.

00:08:03.259 --> 00:08:06.220
Which leads us nicely to the next question.

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:10.099
Wreckuiem asked, “If the clothing around
him is skin, does he shed it?”

00:08:10.099 --> 00:08:14.500
We’re not sure, but it’s definitely a
thought we all wish we could forget.

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:21.009
Now let’s take a look at some of your most
interesting theories.

00:08:21.009 --> 00:08:25.939
Clarence Ilyeme theorized, “Pestilence is
sin and he's trying to take it away.”

00:08:25.939 --> 00:08:28.740
This is certainly an interesting theory.

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:33.229
While we can’t find much in his file that
suggests 049 views The Pestilence as a result

00:08:33.229 --> 00:08:38.250
of sinful behavior or the concept of sin itself,
it’s worth considering that his medical

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:41.510
background seems to come from medieval times.

00:08:41.510 --> 00:08:45.890
Medical science was in its infancy back then,
and many still believed that diseases were

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:51.640
the result of loose morals or even demonic
interference - so there might be some truth

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:52.830
to this theory.

00:08:52.830 --> 00:08:56.420
Thomas Hess theorized, “I feel like he isn't
really bad.

00:08:56.420 --> 00:09:00.100
All he wants to do is help and cure everyone,
but his cure is death.”

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:04.660
If we’re defining bad as “a malicious
desire to cause harm for its own sake”,

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:07.089
then this theory holds a lot of water.

00:09:07.089 --> 00:09:12.640
For all intents and purposes, it does seem
that 049 does genuinely want to cure his patients

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:16.940
of “The Pestilence”, and he does seem
to express remorse when they die.

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:22.860
However, by his own admission, his cure is
imperfect, and he hasn’t found full success

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:25.970
in curing the disease without causing death
yet.

00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:30.140
Cat N Dog Live theorized, “The plague doctor
has seen the end of the world and travels

00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:33.490
in a loop back in time aiming to eventually
stop it.

00:09:33.490 --> 00:09:38.170
The pestilence is the way each human's impact
on the end of the world is and once he touches

00:09:38.170 --> 00:09:42.320
their flesh they realize this and die of the
realization of what they've done.

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:47.650
The plague doctor may be looking for a human
(or an scp) that is pestilence free, for what

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:49.390
reason we don't know...”

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:53.070
We don’t have an awful lot to say about
this one because there’s no real evidence

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:57.820
either way, but given that time travel does
seem to be possible in the SCP Foundation

00:09:57.820 --> 00:10:01.980
universe, it’s a cool possibility that we
definitely can’t rule out.

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:07.270
It does, however, leave a lot of loose ends
about the gaps in 049’s knowledge, such

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:09.920
as the fact he doesn’t know about the Black
Death.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:12.950
Vladimir Lenin theorized, “He’s the best
doctor ever!

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:17.370
He cures depression, pestilence, and sometimes
his patients even come back from the dead!

00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:18.649
five star rating.”

00:10:18.649 --> 00:10:25.080
This is certainly an extremely charitable
way to view SCP-049, one that he himself would

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:27.140
likely very much appreciate.

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:32.490
However, considering he changes his patients
into mindless, zombified mutants, a better

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:36.180
course of action may just be to attend therapy.

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:39.279
Chaotix theorized, “The Pestilence is Death.

00:10:39.279 --> 00:10:42.170
He is literally trying to cure Death.”

00:10:42.170 --> 00:10:48.440
While this could be one interpretation of
why 049 resurrects his patients as zombies,

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:54.070
death is something that affects all living,
non-anomalous humans, and 049 seems to be

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:59.100
selective on which humans it identifies as
being infected with The Pestilence.

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:04.019
As a result, it’s unlikely that The Pestilence
refers to death itself.

00:11:04.019 --> 00:11:11.170
And death is also likely a preferable alternative
to being turned into a zombie by 049’s experimental

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:12.180
treatments.

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:17.579
The Blue Guardien theorized, “The Pestilence
is the entity in our collective unconsciousness

00:11:17.579 --> 00:11:21.360
described in SCP-5000 "Why?"

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:26.410
This is an extremely interesting theory, and
one that could hold water, too.

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:31.500
If you check out our series on SCP-5000, you’ll
find that the Foundation discovered a being

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:35.959
known as “It” hiding inside the collective
unconsciousness of humankind.

00:11:35.959 --> 00:11:40.060
While the Foundation doesn’t know about
this in our dimension, it’s possible that

00:11:40.060 --> 00:11:46.670
SCP-049 does, and simply doesn’t realize
that everyone is infected with it yet.

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:52.920
But if this is the case, and SCP-049 realizes
that the whole world is infected, he’s likely

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:57.960
to become a much more dangerous anomaly that
refuses to cooperate with anyone.

00:11:57.960 --> 00:12:03.970
Moonleafs 430 theorized, “The Pestilence
is the Foundation and 049 is a disciple of

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:05.610
the Scarlet King.”

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:08.170
This is another incredibly fun theory.

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:10.360
However, there are two big problems.

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:15.560
The first is that 049 has historically identified
people with no Foundation affiliation as being

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:17.660
infected with The Pestilence.

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:23.639
And the second, even more important issue
is that SCP-049 is a highly scientific creature,

00:12:23.639 --> 00:12:28.380
whereas the Scarlet King hates the very idea
of science with a burning passion.

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:33.960
As a result, SCP-049 and the Scarlet King
are likely natural enemies.

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:39.060
And finally, Xerthrax theorized “His theme
song should probably be Gangsta's Paradise.

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:41.180
It's just a speculation, though.”

00:12:41.180 --> 00:12:44.870
On this theory, we wholeheartedly agree.

00:12:44.870 --> 00:12:46.280
And there you have it.

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:51.670
Thanks to everybody who sent in their great
questions and theories about SCP-049!

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:55.950
Keep an eye on our community posts to see
what anomalous entity we need your thoughts

00:12:55.950 --> 00:12:57.070
on next!

00:12:57.070 --> 00:13:00.510
Got an SCP you’d really like us to cover
in a video like this in future?

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:02.950
Let us know down in the comments!

00:13:02.950 --> 00:13:07.160
And remember to stay safe and stay healthy
- because if you start feeling a little under

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:13.800
the weather, you can expect a visit from SCP-049
some time soon...

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:18.420
Now check out “SCP-096 - Look At A Picture
Of the Shy Guy In Space?

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:24.050
The Shy Guy Questions and Theories” and
“SCP-082 - Fernand The Cannibal” for more

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:25.890
Foundation mysteries unraveled!

